  ('TL3-15',350,'Instruction','7. Plan and prepare a kayak teaching session','Ensure kayaks are selected and fitted to the client.',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL3-15',360,'Instruction','8. Instruct a group in the skills required for a positive river experience','Teach the accepted and commonly used river communication signals',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL3-15',370,'Instruction','8. Instruct a group in the skills required for a positive river experience','Demonstrate ability to teach confidence activities which must include a capsize with a deck.',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL3-15',380,'Instruction','8. Instruct a group in the skills required for a positive river experience','Demonstrate the ability to teach a sweep roll with a logical progression',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL3-15',390,'Instruction','8. Instruct a group in the skills required for a positive river experience','Demonstrate the ability to teach kayaking strokes on flat water and moving water Forward Forward sweep strokes Draw stroke Edging/railing Eddy turn progression (Driving the boat on edge) Ferry glides and bank to bank ‘S’ turns',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL3-15',400,'Instruction','8. Instruct a group in the skills required for a positive river experience','A logical sequence of progressions.',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL3-15',410,'Instruction','8. Instruct a group in the skills required for a positive river experience','Clear demonstrations and explanations.',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL3-15',420,'Instruction','9. Apply the relevant points of the education and facilitation models','Appropriate brief and define the purpose of the kayaking session',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL3-15',430,'Instruction','9. Apply the relevant points of the education and facilitation models','Run an effective debrief and where appropriate, transfer of learning.',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL3-18',10,'SMS',null,'The climbing is managed within the T1, T2 and T3 requirements',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL3-18',20,'Technical Competence','1. Demonstrate and describe the care and appropriate use of climbing equipment','Use equipment that is in good condition and is well maintained.',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL3-18',30,'Technical Competence','1. Demonstrate and describe the care and appropriate use of climbing equipment','Complete a pre- and post-activity check of equipment for damage.',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL3-18',40,'Technical Competence','1. Demonstrate and describe the care and appropriate use of climbing equipment','Describe the advantages and disadvantages of current equipment used for rock climbing and reasons for choice e.g. - static rope, dynamic rope, tubular tape, fabric properties (spectra vs nylon), abseil devices, prussik cord, harnesses, helmets, karabiner types, manual and auto belay devices.',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL3-18',50,'Technical Competence','1. Demonstrate and describe the care and appropriate use of climbing equipment','Uses equipment in accordance with the manufacturer’s recommendations and current best practice.',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL3-18',60,'Technical Competence','2. Demonstrate competence with rope management, anchor knowledge and gear placement','Demonstrate efficient rope management techniques.',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL3-18',70,'Technical Competence','2. Demonstrate competence with rope management, anchor knowledge and gear placement','Demonstrates a working knowledge of knots that are appropriate to the situation.',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL3-18',80,'Technical Competence','2. Demonstrate competence with rope management, anchor knowledge and gear placement','Demonstrate the use and limitations of edge kits',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL3-18',90,'Technical Competence','2. Demonstrate competence with rope management, anchor knowledge and gear placement','Demonstrate a thorough understanding of placed protection e.g. wires, stoppers, hexes, camming devices.',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL3-18',100,'Technical Competence','2. Demonstrate competence with rope management, anchor knowledge and gear placement','Demonstrate a thorough understanding of fixed protection, and how to test e.g. bolts, chains, waratahs, trees and threads.',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL3-18',110,'Technical Competence','2. Demonstrate competence with rope management, anchor knowledge and gear placement','Construct multi-point anchors for top-rope and abseil that minimise shock loading, share the load, have minimal angles, have redundancy, are multi-directional if required, allow ropes to run smoothly and minimise wear.',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL3-18',120,'Technical Competence','2. Demonstrate competence with rope management, anchor knowledge and gear placement','Demonstrate an understanding of forces, fall factors, strength and limitations of gear',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL3-18',130,'Technical Competence','2. Demonstrate competence with rope management, anchor knowledge and gear placement','Construct at least two multi-directional anchor systems which demonstrate the use of: · Placed protection e.g. wires, stoppers, hexes, camming devices. · Fixed protection e.g. bolts, chains, waratahs, bollards, trees or threads. · Linking multi-point anchors (defined as 3 or more). · Allow ropes to run smoothly and minimise wear',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL3-18',140,'Technical Competence','3. Demonstrate efficient and safe personal climbing and belay skills','Leading a grade 18 on placed protection',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL3-18',150,'Technical Competence','3. Demonstrate efficient and safe personal climbing and belay skills','Demonstrate safe and efficient lead and belay technique using double ropes.',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL3-18',160,'Technical Competence','3. Demonstrate efficient and safe personal climbing and belay skills','Demonstrate lead, then top belay off the anchors.',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL3-18',170,'Technical Competence','4. Demonstrate crag rescue skills','Demonstrate ascending and descending a fixed line, utilising a mechanical device e.g. gri-gri, ID',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL3-18',180,'Technical Competence','4. Demonstrate crag rescue skills','Demonstrate the ability to abseil multiple clients, without exposing clients to any harm? E.g. stacking',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL3-18',190,'Technical Competence','4. Demonstrate crag rescue skills','Demonstrate the ability to lower clients down a climb using a Reverso or similar manual auto-locking device.',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL3-18',200,'Technical Competence','4. Demonstrate crag rescue skills','Demonstrate the ability to abseil with an injured or scared climber.',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL3-18',210,'Technical Competence','4. Demonstrate crag rescue skills','Demonstrate raising a climber using an assisted hoist and then an unassisted hoist',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL3-18',220,'The Environment','5. Demonstrate and role model environmental knowledge and practice','Role model the NZAC code of Conduct for Rock Climbers',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL3-18',230,'The Environment','5. Demonstrate and role model environmental knowledge and practice','Observe any changes to the weather and modify the session if necessary.',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL3-18',240,'The Environment','5. Demonstrate and role model environmental knowledge and practice','Provide interpretive information about: · The natural and cultural history of the area. · The geology of the climbing site. · Local flora and fauna.',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL3-18',250,'Group Management and Leadership','6. Lead and manage a group leading on single pitch climbs','Supervising and coaching climbers and belayers and never compromise personal or client safety',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL3-18',260,'Group Management and Leadership','6. Lead and manage a group leading on single pitch climbs','Leadership style appropriate to the participants and the environment',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL3-18',270,'Group Management and Leadership','6. Lead and manage a group leading on single pitch climbs','Establish a rapport and have an awareness of their emotional and cultural needs',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL3-18',280,'Group Management and Leadership','6. Lead and manage a group leading on single pitch climbs','Manage participants safety effectively both climbing and descending',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL3-18',290,'Group Management and Leadership','7. Demonstrate effective safety management.','Manage participants safety with route selection, appropriate gear and safety checks',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL3-18',300,'Group Management and Leadership','7. Demonstrate effective safety management.','Demonstrate checking routes used for hazards and demonstrate risk management principles to minimize or avoid the impact of any identified hazards.',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL3-18',310,'Group Management and Leadership','7. Demonstrate effective safety management.','Use an effective communication system and a systematic checking system with participants',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL3-18',320,'Group Management and Leadership','7. Demonstrate effective safety management.','Demonstrate safe practices ad good judgement and decision making with the scope of the competency',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL3-18',330,'Instruction','8. Plan and prepare a rock skills day.','Have a clearly defined purpose and a session appropriate for the group',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL3-18',340,'Instruction','8. Plan and prepare a rock skills day.','Describe emergency procedures that may be required if a serious incident occurred',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL3-18',350,'Instruction','8. Plan and prepare a rock skills day.','Placing protection and runners for lead climbing',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL3-18',360,'Instruction','8. Plan and prepare a rock skills day.','Efficient and safe belaying of a lead climber including clear communication between climbing partners',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL3-18',370,'Instruction','8. Plan and prepare a rock skills day.','Efficient and safe abseil techniques demonstrating personal safety using a prusik and bottom (fireman’s) belay',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL3-18',380,'Instruction','8. Plan and prepare a rock skills day.','A logical sequence of progressions.',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL3-18',390,'Instruction','8. Plan and prepare a rock skills day.','Clear demonstrations and explanations.',true,true,true,true,false,false),
