  ('TL4-07',10,'SMS',null,'The river trip is managed within the T1, T2 and T3 requirements',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-07',20,'Technical Competence','1. Demonstrate the care and correct use of canoeing gear and equipment',' Use equipment that is in good condition and well maintained and used in accordance with the manufacturer’s recommendations and current best practice  Carry and demonstrate and/or describe the use and care of safety equipment appropriate to the conditions for a safe and successful day trip e.g. towlines, VHF radio, Satellite phone, Personal Locater Beacon, throw bags, buoyancy, survival bags, slings, karabiners, Prussic, pullies, knife, saw, spare paddle, bailer and painters,  Complete a pre-activity check of equipment and describe how to identify worn or damaged equipment  Be able to carry out basic field repairs and provide the means to do so',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-07',30,'Technical Competence','2. Demonstrate personal canoeing skills on class 2',' A range of efficient and effective paddling techniques both tandem and solo from all four quadrants of the canoe e.g. forward, reverse, J-stroke, cross-bow draw, draw and pry strokes, low bracing, static and dynamic strokes  Controlled Eddy turns holding tilt  Forward and reverse ferry gliding  Safe and efficient river running including choosing dry lines /routes down rapids.  Trim  Lining (down river)  Portaging',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-07',40,'Technical Competence','2. Demonstrate personal canoeing skills on class 2',' Packing for a multi-day trip  Canoe loading for windy conditions  Water displacement',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-07',50,'Technical Competence','3. Demonstrate river rescue skills.','Self-Rescue:  Swim to shore with fully loaded canoe using painter or throw bag then bail the canoe  Right a fully loaded boat and re-entry without shore access',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-07',60,'Technical Competence','3. Demonstrate river rescue skills.','Boat Based Rescue:  Tow canoe (short and long systems)  X-rescue  Curl  Effectively manage the group while dealing with a canoe over (multiple swimmer)  Rescue of an unconscious swimmer',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-07',70,'Technical Competence','3. Demonstrate river rescue skills.','Use of a throw bag to:  Rescue a swimmer - attention gained, accurate throw, stable belay, safe pendulum  Set up a simple hauling system / Z- drag / 3:1 system and pig-rig, with a pin kit. (For efficiency this can be done as a simulated rescue on land)',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-07',80,'Technical Competence','3. Demonstrate river rescue skills.','Describe methods for dealing with:  Foot entrapments',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-07',90,'The Environment','4. Apply weather interpretation and forecasting skills',' Weather signs when in the field e.g.: cloud types, wind speed, wind direction, temperature and anticipate weather conditions',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-07',100,'The Environment','5. Role model accepted environmental practices',' Role model the principles of the New Zealand Water Care Code, the New Zealand Environmental Care Code and/or Leave No Trace',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-07',110,'The Environment','6. Demonstrate and / or describe cultural and environmental knowledge and interpretation of sites visited',' The natural and cultural history of the area  The geology of the area',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-07',120,'Group Management and Leadership','7. Plan and prepare for a multi-day instructional and guided trip',' Map showing proposed route, estimated travel times and distances, points of interest, hazards  Hazard identification and risk management strategies e.g. RAMS, AMP, SAPS  Two relevant weather maps and analyses on which you are basing your proposed trip  Detailed contingency plan and alternate routes  Access details and contact phone numbers e.g. DOC, Local Iwi, Regional Council, Landowners, Metphone, Metfax, Coastguard, Marine VHF Channels for emergency and weather forecast  Gear and equipment lists for individuals and the group  A menu plan which includes balanced, nutritious and varied food, fuel requirements, emergency food and identifies safe methods for organising group cooking',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-07',130,'Group Management and Leadership','7. Plan and prepare for a multi-day instructional and guided trip',' A safety brief before the session or river trip commences  A range of on the water group management strategies as appropriate  Effective and proactive management of the group including: anticipation of capsizes, dealing with differences in abilities of party members, protecting rapids as appropriate  An effective communication system for managing the group  Establishing rapport and using a leadership style appropriate to the group',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-07',140,'Group Management and Leadership','7. Plan and prepare for a multi-day instructional and guided trip',' Awareness of the risks and appropriate risk management strategies during a given session or river trip and the ability to adjust plans when required  Safe practices and good judgement and decision making within the scope of this qualification',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-07',150,'Instruction','10. Prepare and deliver teaching sessions',' The selection and preparation of a suitable location or venue appropriate to the lesson  A range of teaching skills e.g. introduction, appropriate voice, language and body language, teaching/visual aids, demonstrations, teachable moments, evaluation of learning',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-07',160,'Instruction','10. Prepare and deliver teaching sessions',' Engaging the students in a positive learning experience which encourages enthusiasm and interest',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-07',170,'Instruction','11. Teach moving water skills',' Pack a canoe for a multi-day river trip with reference to distribution, trim, lashing, accessibility  Selecting a suitable training site  Preparing and delivering a safe, well managed and positive learning experience  Eddy turns  Ferry gliding',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-07',180,'Instruction','12. Teach river running skills',' Selecting a suitable river trip  Preparing and delivering a safe, well managed and positive learning experience  Identifying river features and hazards and how to use and/or avoid them  Effective communication including the use of paddle signals  River running strategies, including scouting and choosing safe lines through rapids or lining down rapids',true,true,true,true,false,false),
